{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OPERATOR RULING (2026-08-21): option (a) APPROVED — persist close provenance durably. Record the gate-state/close-provenance in the close STATUS event itself (event-schema addition) so a later reader can distinguish: gate-off close, --force close (with its reason — note txn.transition_core currently discards force_close_reason, tracked separately under defiant-orthoclase-buck; coordinate, don't duplicate), local unattested close, certifiable-false withholding, and signature-append failure. The audit sidecar remains an audit surface, not the discriminator. Implementation must follow docs/event-schema.md and docs/migrations.md (additive, reducer-known, backward-compatible with historical events that lack the field)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787352366797572001,"uuid":"adb6f7c5-8e58-440f-9cb5-f9324b18d04a"}